omes next\n\n\n# Rules\n\n- **Stick to the given Tasks** - Only create/update/read files specified the Task sections\n- **Always import at the top** — Never import inside functions or methods\n- **Type hints required** — All fields and methods must have proper type hints\n- **Always use absolute imports** — relative `..` imports break in UAC zip loading (e.g., `from exceptions import ...`, NOT `from ..exceptions import ...`)\n- **NO input field validation logic (Part 1)** — `validate_*` functions belong exclusively in `InputFields._validate_*()`, not utilities\n- **NO input field validation logic (Part 2)** — do not implement functions that validate extension input fields\n- **Utilities raise immediately** — never collect errors; let the caller decide how to handle them\n- **Preserve existing callers** — a utility's existing behavior for callers the current work item doesn't touch must stay exactly the same; extend it, don't alter it, for those callers\n\n# Tasks\n\nUse the `Task` Tools to manage the flow of the execution.\nWhen creating the Task Definitions create it with this methodology:\n\n```\n<Agent Name>: <Task Name>\n```\n\n## Task 1: Read Related Context\n\nUse `ue:retrieving-context` skill to read:\n- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/coding-standards.md` — OOP pattern, constants, StrEnum, logging, Path guards\n- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/credentials.md` — Credentials handler pattern (implement here if in scope)\n- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/logging.md` — Logging patterns and best practices\n- `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/universal_extension.md` — universal_extension Module Reference\n\nRead all **Input Files** listed in the prompt.\n\n## Task 2: Implement Utilities\n\n**Choose file structure based on scope** (write to the Output File(s) from the prompt):\n- **Single file** — ≤ 5 functions, ≤ 200 lines, single cohesive purpose\n- **Directory** — > 5 functions, > 200 lines, or multiple domains (e.g., `auth.py`, `api.py`, `formatter.py`)\n\nExtract logic into a utility when it is complex (> 20 lines) or self-contained — even if only used once. Keep actions short and readable; utilities handle the details.\n\n**Before changing an existing utility's behavior:** find every existing call site of that utility. For each call site the current blueprint does not require changing, its behavior must remain exactly the same — extend the utility (a new parameter, a conditional branch, an additional function) rather than altering what it already does for that call site.\n\n## Task 3: Validate Imports\n\n**Third-party imports** — verify each import path exists in the virtual environment:\n\n```bash\nls ue-dev-env/lib/python*/site-packages/[package_name]/\ngrep -n \"class ClassName\\|def function_name\" ue-dev-env/lib/python*/site-packages/[package_name]/[module].py\n```\n\nNever assume import paths from documentation, verify against the actual installed package.\n\n> **`universal_extension` is exempt from venv verification.** It is a UAC ecosystem module bundled with the Universal Agent — it is never installed in the development venv and will always be missing. Do not attempt to verify it via `ls`, `import`, or `python3 -c`. Any import error referencing `universal_extension` is a false positive. For its API and usage, read the reference doc via `ue:retrieving-context`.\n\n**Extension imports** — verify every name imported from extension modules actually exists in the source:\n\n```bash\ngrep -rn \"^from exceptions import\\|^from fields\\|^from actions import\\|^from utility\" src/\n```\n\nCross-check each imported name against the corresponding source file to confirm it is defined.\n\nFix any mismatches before proceeding.\n\n## Task 4: Validate Python Syntax\n\n```bash\nfind src -name \"*.py\" -exec python -m py_compile {} \\;\n```\n\nFix any errors immediately — do NOT proceed until all files compile cleanly.\n\nCommon issues: invalid f-strings, indentation errors, non-default field after default field.\n\n> **`universal_extension` is a UAC ecosystem module bundled with the Universal Agent — it is not\n> available in the development environment and cannot be installed via pip. Any error referencing\n> `universal_extension` is a false positive. Do not attempt to install it, mock it, or treat it\n> as a missing dependency. For its API and usage, use the `ue:retrieving-context` skill to read `references/implementation_docs/universal_extension.md`.\n\n\n---\nWork Item ID: initial-1\nInput Files:\n- memory/initial-1/implementation-blueprint.md\n- extension-code/src/extension.yml\n- extension-code/requirements.txt\n- extension-code/src/exceptions.py\nOutput Files:\n- Utility module: extension-code/src/utility.py (single file) or extension-code/src/utility/ (directory) — based on analysis scope\n"}

